    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "The rendered HTML from Vue has additional whitespace in contrast with React or plain JS. This will cause issues later on when creating inline snapshots.\r\n\r\nThis empty comment `<!-- -->` makes sure no additional whitespace is rendered here.\r\n\r\nI'm not fond of this approach, but the alternative is modifying our serializer to ignore empty lines / whitespaces.\r\n\r\nWdyt?",
    "commit_id": "30d25648d39ee2d53e18a0b0b65f45512ca38ba6",
    "created_at": "2023-06-12T14:57:46Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -24,26 +24,32 @@\n           >\n             <slot name=\"rootLabel\">Home</slot>\n           </a>\n-          <span v-else>\n+          <a\n+            v-else\n+            :href=\"state.createURL(null)\"\n+            :class=\"suit('link')\"\n+            @click.prevent=\"state.refine(null)\"\n+          >\n             <slot name=\"rootLabel\">Home</slot>\n-          </span>\n-        </li>\n-        <li\n+          </a>\n+          <!-- eslint-disable prettier/prettier -->\n+        </li><!--\n+        --><li\n           v-for=\"(item, index) in state.items\"\n           :key=\"item.label\"\n           :class=\"[suit('item'), isLastItem(index) && suit('item', 'selected')]\"\n         >\n+          <!-- eslint-enable prettier/prettier -->",
